[{:draft 1,
  :overall 6.8,
  :passes false,
  :errors [],
  :scores
  {:A
   {:score 6,
    :reason
    "The creature voices are light and plain (\"Leash is right there.\", \"Jar's looking far away.\"), and no film lines or job titles appear. Several lines break the twin rule, though. Hal claims the memorial move the player made (\"I moved {name} to memorial.\"), plaques invent traits for any pet (\"Slept in every sunny spot.\"), and some bubbles assert state the estate doesn't track (\"Manger's empty.\", \"Nice day for a nap.\"). Biscuit's own bubble also speaks to Biscuit (\"Walk, Bisco?\").",
    :violations
    [{:where
      ":modes :memorial :hal-note line 2 \"I moved {name} to memorial...\" and line 4 \"I've set {name} up in memorial...\"",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "GDD §2.5 says only the player moves a pet to memorial, and this note fires when they do. Hal claiming the act is untrue to what really happened.",
      :fix
      "\"You've moved {name} to memorial. Nothing's due from them now, ever.\""}
     {:where
      ":modes :memorial :hal-note line 4 \"I've set {name} up in memorial. Nothing's expected of them anymore, only remembered.\"",
      :rule 1,
      :issue
      "It reads like an administrator closing a ticket, not a companion at a loss. The second sentence is also ungrammatical (\"Nothing's expected... only remembered\").",
      :fix
      "\"I'm sorry. {name}'s in the sun now, and nothing's asked of them.\""}
     {:where
      ":modes :memorial :plaque lines 2, 3, 5 (\"Slept in every sunny spot.\", \"Followed everywhere, loyally.\", \"A steady, gentle friend.\")",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "These invent a personality for any memorial pet. In GDD §2.5 personality is the player's own words, declared per creature, and a generic plaque can't know them.",
      :fix
      "Keep plaques to what is known: \"{name}, {years}. Loved.\" / \"{name}, {years}. Still here in the sun.\" / \"For {name}, {years}.\""}
     {:where
      ":juniper :hungry \"Manger's empty.\" and \"Nosing the gate.\"",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "The mirror tracks only the 12-hour hay chore and a bale count. An empty manger and a gate are invented state, not the creature's real state (pillar 'real, not simulated').",
      :fix
      "\"Twelve hours. Hay?\" / \"Hay time, no?\" (keep that one)."}
     {:where ":biscuit :porch \"Nice day for a nap.\"",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "The sky follows the clock (estate.edn :sky), so this can show at blue hour or night. It claims weather the estate doesn't report.",
      :fix "\"Good spot for a nap.\""}
     {:where ":biscuit :walk-due \"Walk, Bisco?\"",
      :rule 2,
      :issue
      "This is Biscuit's own bubble, but it addresses Bisco, so it reads as the player or twin talking to the dog. The bubble should speak to you.",
      :fix "\"Leash, door, you?\""}]},
   :B
   {:score 8,
    :reason
    "The chores match the mirrors: Flora's worms and jar, Juniper's hay and bales, Biscuit at the door by his leash. The :hungry lines stay one steady, unescalating ask (\"Worms, please?\", \"Hay, please?\", \"Walk time?\"), which respects the pressure ceiling. The memorial notes never tell the player plainly that the pet's chores are off their list, and §2.5 says the twin does say so.",
    :violations
    [{:where ":modes :memorial :hal-note (all five)",
      :rule 6,
      :issue
      "GDD §2.5: a pet moved to memorial stops counting toward 'your own chores done' and the twin says so. The lines only imply it (\"No tasks, no tending\"). They never tell the player the day no longer waits on that chore.",
      :fix
      "Give at least one variant the plain fact: \"{name}'s in memorial. Their chores are off your list now; nothing's due.\""}
     {:where ":flora :fed \"Worms: delivered.\"",
      :rule 6,
      :issue
      "Feeding is a real chore the player does by hand (the snap moment, GDD §2.2). 'Delivered' frames it as a courier drop-off, not the moment the player just had with Flora.",
      :fix "\"Snap. Got it.\""}]},
   :C
   {:score 9,
    :reason
    "There are no scores, streaks or points. Nothing shames a missed feeding, nobody real is named, and no line claims a purchase or message. No memorial line speaks as if the pet were alive (\"{name} doesn't need anything from us now.\"). One memorial note tells the player how to feel about their loss.",
    :violations
    [{:where
      ":modes :memorial :hal-note line 2 \"They're remembered now, not tended to — and that's right.\"",
      :rule 12,
      :issue
      "'And that's right' passes judgment on the player's grief and decision. Kind and truthful means stating what changed, not ruling on it.",
      :fix
      "\"You've moved {name} to memorial. Remembered now, not tended.\""}]},
   :D
   {:score 5,
    :reason
    "Every line is bubble-length and the {stock}/{bales} placeholders avoid the '1 worms' trap. But the signs are one line reworded five times (\"Worms: {stock}\", \"Worm jar: {stock}\", \"Jar count: {stock}\"), some read as inventory software (\"Stock: {stock}\", \"Low stock: {stock}\"), and lines repeat across creatures. Several placeholder lines break for some values or species.",
    :violations
    [{:where ":flora :stock-sign and :juniper :stock-sign (all ten)",
      :rule 18,
      :issue
      "Every variant is 'label: {count}', which is the same line reworded, not real variety.",
      :fix
      "Vary what the hand-lettered sign says: \"Flora's worms: {stock}\" / \"{stock} in the jar\" / \"Worm jar · {stock}\" / \"Hay pile: {bales}\" / \"{bales} bales in the barn\"."}
     {:where ":flora :low and :juniper :low",
      :rule 18,
      :issue
      "The low signs reword each other and the everyday sign. \"Hay stock: {bales}\" appears in both :low and :stock-sign, so a low pile looks no different from a full one. \"Running low — {x} left\" is copied across both creatures.",
      :fix
      "Make each :low variant say 'low' differently, and none match a :stock-sign: \"Only {stock} in the jar\" / \"Worms low: {stock}\" / \"Hay's thin: {bales}\" / \"{bales} bales. Restock?\"."}
     {:where
      ":flora :fed \"That hit the spot.\" and :biscuit :walked \"That hit the spot.\"",
      :rule 18,
      :issue
      "The same line is reused across two creatures, and as a food idiom it doesn't fit a walk.",
      :fix "Biscuit :walked: \"Sniffed everything. Good walk.\""}
     {:where
      ":biscuit :porch \"Watching the yard.\" and \"Keeping watch.\"",
      :rule 18,
      :issue "These two variants say the same thing.",
      :fix "Replace one: \"Sun's on the porch boards.\""}
     {:where
      ":flora :stock-sign \"Stock: {stock}\", :flora :low \"Low stock: {stock}\", :juniper :stock-sign \"On hand: {bales}\"",
      :rule 17,
      :issue
      "These are warehouse labels on what the request calls hand-lettered signs. That is corporate, not the cozy diorama voice.",
      :fix "\"Worms left: {stock}\" / \"Bales in the barn: {bales}\"."}
     {:where
      ":flora :low \"Running low — {stock} left\" and :juniper :low \"Running low — {bales} left\"",
      :rule 19,
      :issue
      ":low fires at <= 2, which includes 0, and \"Running low — 0 left\" is wrong: the supply is out, not low.",
      :fix "\"Worms left: {stock}\". It reads correctly at 2, 1 or 0."}
     {:where
      ":modes :memorial :plaque line 1 \"{name}, {years}. A good dog, missed.\"",
      :rule 19,
      :issue
      "Memorial is a mode for any creature (§2.5). With {name} = an axolotl or a horse, 'a good dog' is wrong.",
      :fix "\"{name}, {years}. Good company, missed.\""}
     {:where
      ":modes :virtual :idle line 5 \"{name}'s content, watching the water.\"",
      :rule 19,
      :issue
      "A virtual creature can live on the porch or in the barn. 'Watching the water' only reads right for one at the canal.",
      :fix "\"{name}'s content, just watching.\""}
     {:where
      ":modes :memorial :plaque line 3 \"{name}, {years}. Followed everywhere, loyally.\"",
      :rule 19,
      :issue
      "'Followed everywhere' has no object, so the line doesn't read correctly. It also assumes a following animal.",
      :fix "\"{name}, {years}. Always nearby.\""}]},
   :S
   {:score 5,
    :reason
    "A few details are Prime Meridian's own: the worm jar, the leash by the door, the hay count. Most lines could sit in any cozy pet game (\"Full and happy.\", \"Better now.\", \"All good here.\", \"Settled in.\"). None touch the estate's places (canal, porch, barn), Flora's 5 pm feed, the 12-hour hay round, or the fact that the twin, not the pet, carries the memorial news.",
    :violations
    [{:where ":flora :hungry and :fed (most variants)",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "Generic hunger and fullness lines. Nothing ties them to Flora's canal, her jar on the bank, or her 5 pm feed.",
      :fix
      "\"Five o'clock. Jar's on the bank.\" / \"Canal's quiet. Worm?\" / :fed \"Snap. Back to the weeds.\""}
     {:where
      ":juniper :fed (\"That's better.\", \"Full now.\", \"Settled in.\")",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "These lines could belong to any horse in any game. They don't mention the barn or the 12-hour rhythm.",
      :fix "\"Good hay. See you in twelve.\" / \"Barn's quiet now.\""}
     {:where
      ":biscuit :porch \"All good here.\", :modes :virtual :idle \"{name}'s around, no fuss.\"",
      :rule 3,
      :issue
      "These are placeholder-generic idles with no sense of the estate.",
      :fix
      "\"Porch boards are warm.\" / \"{name}'s here for the company, nothing more.\""}]}}}
 {:draft 2,
